Let clients send files-api's own fields (language, parse_method, metadata, raw,
...) through the proxy, and get the fields it adds to file objects back.

The proxy drops upload form fields and query parameters it does not know, the
OpenAI files retrieve, delete, and list calls take no extra_query, and
OpenAIFileObject drops unknown response fields. These fields are files-api's,
not OpenAI's, so this is not an upstream bug.

On upload, content, retrieve, delete, and list, pass every form field and query
parameter except the proxy's own upload, routing, and logging fields to the
OpenAI SDK as extra_body and extra_query. They never become LiteLLM call
kwargs, and `expires_after` keeps the team's enforced expiry. List pagination
(limit, after, order) reaches the backend as well. Keep extra fields on file
objects.

Checks: tests/verify_files_extra_fields.py

